  "summary": "This study prepared Ti3C2Tx by LiF/HCl (MILD) etching and exfoliation, then compared pristine, acid-crumpled (C-MXene), oxidized-co-crumpled (OC-MXene), and over-oxidized (OO-MXene) electrodes. C-MXene differs through H2SO4-induced low-pH flocculation, whereas OC-MXene additionally receives controlled H2O2 oxidation; OO-MXene uses excessive oxidation and becomes largely TiO2-like. OC-MXene was the headline electrode, delivering 307 F/g at 2 mV/s in 1 M H2SO4, with a BET surface area of 72 m2/g and mesopores of 2\u201320 nm. The paper did not report electrode thickness, mass loading, areal/volumetric capacitance, or numerical capacitances for the three non-primary electrodes."
